[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-35]  Attributed to multiple references:  [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-Etkind-31]  [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-h710-32]  [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-q611-33]  [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-v008-34]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-603]  At least 176 foreign civilians from 25 countries are confirmed to have been killed within Ukraine.  [LINK: (See table here) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_War#Foreign_civilians]  for a detailed breakdown of deaths by nationalities.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-609]   [LINK: (See here) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Russo-Ukrainian_War#Civilian_deaths]  for a detailed breakdown of civilian deaths by oblast, according to Ukrainian authorities.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-612]  Some civilians have been reported to have died in captivity in Russia, [LINK: ([603]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-610]  like journalist  [LINK: (Victoria Roshchyna) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_Roshchyna] . [LINK: ([604]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-611]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-617]  The DPR stated 1,799 of its civilians were killed and 6,902 wounded in its territories between 1 January 2022 and 22 December 2024, [LINK: ([607]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-615]  of which 8 died and 23 were wounded between 1 January and 25 February 2022, [LINK: ([608]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-ombudsman1-616]  leaving a total of 1,791 killed and 6,879 wounded in the period of the Russian invasion.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-missing_627-0]  63,000 missing as of 17 February 2025. [LINK: ([616]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-625]  90 percent of which were thought to be soldiers, [LINK: ([617]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-626]  which would be around 56,700.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-DPRK_634-0]  In addition, Ukraine claimed six  [LINK: (North Korean) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Korea]  soldiers were killed in a missile strike in early October 2024, while fighting alongside Russian forces.  [LINK: (South Korea's Defense Minister) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_National_Defense_(South_Korea)]  said of this report it was "highly likely" true. [LINK: ([622]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-632]  However, Russia denied the reports. [LINK: ([623]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-633]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_ref-713]  Most likely, new cities meant new industrial cities in Siberia, the construction plans of which were announced by Shoigu in the fall of 2021. [LINK: ([701]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022%E2%80%93present)#cite_note-712]


